# {{ project_name }}

pnpm + Turbo monorepo: NestJS API (modular monolith, kernel-only — modules are catalog
entries installed via `pnpm platform module add`) + headless {% if web_stack == 'next' %}React/Next.js{% else %}React/Vite{% endif %} web (transport +
access guard only; UI kit is the product's choice), HTTP contract via Zod → OpenAPI →
generated Kubb client. Generated from `platform-template` — upstream changes arrive via
`copier update` (see [`docs/dev/template.md`](docs/dev/template.md)); a newer template tag
or a fix landing on an installed catalog entry surfaces at session start via the
template-behind and pending-advisories hooks — the routine is the `template-update` skill.
Version truth for the template itself is the git tag + [`template-changelog.md`](docs/dev/template-changelog.md),
never `package.json`.

**This file routes; it does not argue.** Every rule lives in a skill; this file is the map
to it, never the rule itself.

## Two standing rules

**Think and work in English; answer the user in {{ product_locale }}, explaining from the business
side.** {{ product_locale }} is for user-facing replies only — thinking, subagent prompts and internal
notes stay in English. → [`.agents/skills/communication/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/communication/SKILL.md)

**Disk is the source of truth for what exists.** The skills describe the target
architecture, and this file keeps no inventory — static inventories rot. Before
referencing a module, file or package, check disk (`ls apps/api/src/modules`,
`ls packages`, the tree in `apps/web/src`).

